        "Meter glitches (opsd.py). Any quarter-hour above 10 times the series' 99.9th percentile is treated as a counter jump, removed and filled in. Gaps up to 2 hours (8 steps) are interpolated; a longer gap breaks the series, and only the longest unbroken stretch is kept. Energy per quarter-hour × 4 = average kW over that quarter-hour {gi_code_opsd}.",
        "Prices (energycharts.py). Only from 1 October 2025, when the day-ahead market moved to 15-minute products {sdac_15min}. EUR per MWh ÷ 1,000 = EUR per kWh; duplicate timestamps are dropped and missing quarter-hours filled by straight-line interpolation. Each API response states its licence; a zone without 'CC BY' raises an error and is skipped {gi_code_ec}.",
